sh, and Alex Fan. Videos of their dance routines have split fans, with critics calling the performances gross and questioning their fit for NFL audiences, while supporters emphasize talent and auditions over gender. This follows a league trend, as eleven teams now include male cheerleaders or stunt performers, sparking talks on evolving sports entertainment.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T01:42:31.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108327748468871169"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108514511129137251"},{"post_id":"2108489214639640873"},{"post_id":"2108495938897489961"},{"post_id":"2108567239997669698"},{"post_id":"2108490720541639083"},{"post_id":"2108408930825023679"},{"post_id":"2108499432211955866"},{"post_id":"2108514638916665366"},{"post_id":"2108473520380322297"},{"post_id":"2108485106398900328"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Soccer"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108571012283482507","name":"Users on X Share Sportybet and Betpawa Betting Codes for High-Odds Football Accumulators","summary":"Multiple posts on X feature alphanumeric codes such as 9BSKYN, CXLR5P, and P64RY7 for use on Sportybet and Betpawa platforms. These codes promote betting slips with odds ranging from 10 to over 100, targeting today's and weekend football matches. Users encourage participation with phrases like 'Good luck' and share screenshots of their accumulator bets.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T15:11:19.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108571012283482507"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108220550044594597"},{"post_id":"2108324186112377042"},{"post_id":"2108278946273837056"},{"post_id":"2108345453813137806"},{"post_id":"2108360853221507406"},{"post_id":"2108278946273837056"},{"post_id":"2108220550044594597"},{"post_id":"2108324186112377042"},{"post_id":"2108345453813137806"},{"post_id":"2108346543677870107"}],"contexts":{"topics":["NBA"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Chicago Bulls fans spot the team's logo shrunk small on new black warmup jackets, overshadowed by a giant red-outlined Plus500 Trading emblem on the chest.","id":"2108368895732277319","name":"Bulls Fans Upset Over Sponsor-Dominated Warmup Jackets","summary":"The jackets, part of a 2022 sponsorship deal with the London-based fintech firm, place the trading company's circular logo boldly above the smaller Bulls crest. Fans contrast the look with classic white Jordan-era gear, where the team emblem took center stage, dubbing the new ones 'Plus500 Trading Bulls.' One fan summed it up: 'The Bulls used to be the logo. Now they’re just the fine print.' The backlash taps into wider concerns about sponsors eclipsing team identity in pro sports.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:40:49.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108368895732277319"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108480106532643041"},{"post_id":"2108475259645260208"},{"post_id":"2108398319265529889"},{"post_id":"2108481116738871466"},{"post_id":"2108464223286448279"},{"post_id":"2108500624228667682"},{"post_id":"2108427160621142351"},{"post_id":"2108491057000292778"},{"post_id":"2108391834498281958"},{"post_id":"2108464660886237250"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Soccer"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108514670709772571","name":"Lionel Messi retires from football","summary":"Lionel Messi has retired from football. Discussions on X focus on this retirement in the context of the Messi vs Ronaldo GOAT debate, with fans comparing their careers, statistics, achievements including World Cups and Olympic gold, and referencing Ronaldo's comment on Messi's post.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T12:17:15.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108514670709772571"},{"category":"News","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108585533395931490"},{"post_id":"2108585511828779154"},{"post_id":"2108585715663794670"},{"post_id":"2108595655207682278"},{"post_id":"2108585661557088418"},{"post_id":"2108631193587487091"},{"post_id":"2108588676469154266"},{"post_id":"2108590561498427650"},{"post_id":"2108526562790547757"},{"post_id":"2108588461129396526"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Sports"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108593983790149851","name":"Nigerian Bettors Demand SportyBet Pay Withheld Winnings to 114 Customers Totaling Nearly ₦1 Billion After Almost Two Years","summary":"Numerous Nigerian customers report that SportyBet has not paid their legitimate betting winnings for nearly two years, affecting 114 individuals with nearly ₦1 billion involved. Bettors are demanding transparency from SportyBet and regulatory intervention to investigate complaints against betting companies in Nigeria. SportyBet has responded to some users by requesting direct messages with ticket details for review.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T21:15:58.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108593983790149851"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108591558912045481"},{"post_id":"2108566792717164554"},{"post_id":"2108599239408546230"},{"post_id":"2108570927411696120"},{"post_id":"2108577055193371022"},{"post_id":"2108597298188210400"},{"post_id":"2108605959740465409"},{"post_id":"2108614861483892802"},{"post_id":"2108582384270495894"},{"post_id":"2108629148923314628"}],"contexts":{"topics":["NFL"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108626070421537083","name":"Debate on X over hiring professional Madden players as NFL coaches for situational football decisions","summary":"Users on X are debating a suggestion to hire expert Madden players to advise NFL coaches on late-game situations, clock management, and play-calling due to frequent coaching errors. Critics argue that video game experience does not translate to real football because of factors like player conditioning, heart, and physical execution absent in simulations. Some users see potential value in gamers' analytics-like input, with references to past blunders such as Antonio Pierce's field goal decision.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T20:10:57.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108626070421537083"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108488502300365189"},{"post_id":"2108467873844957392"},{"post_id":"2108509730490499163"},{"post_id":"2108527907673182211"},{"post_id":"2108501245954847024"},{"post_id":"2108539371377086644"},{"post_id":"2108477090366718224"},{"post_id":"2108472921962488246"},{"post_id":"2108527014449971386"},{"post_id":"2108524324428681251"}],"contexts":{"topics":["MLB"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108540169888706833","name":"Debate Over Los Angeles Dodgers' High Spending and Success in MLB Postseason","summary":"Fans and commentators discuss the Los Angeles Dodgers' large payroll, team-friendly contracts, and dominance in baseball amid their postseason advancement. Critics accuse the Dodgers of ruining the sport through excessive spending, while supporters highlight wise investments, a strong farm system, and market advantages. Comparisons are made to other large-market teams and the lack of small-market World Series winners since 2015.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T12:53:18.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108540169888706833"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108607175400759743"},{"post_id":"2108654094751846753"},{"post_id":"2108652469417033899"},{"post_id":"2108659118445666727"},{"post_id":"2108669647319105617"},{"post_id":"2108650068660363517"},{"post_id":"2108659722681503767"},{"post_id":"2108716508952350773"},{"post_id":"2108630637171106068"},{"post_id":"2108652958816809108"}],"contexts":{"topics":["American Football"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","id":"2108656886170206255","name":"Ohio Stadium Announces Sale of Exclusive Football Helmet Popcorn Buckets at Upcoming Game","summary":"Ohio Stadium will sell limited-edition football helmet-shaped popcorn buckets exclusively at Saturday's game.","updated_at":"2026-10-10T01:33:35.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108656886170206255"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2107557410827387140"},{"post_id":"2108235628693664241"},{"post_id":"2108037675714293829"},{"post_id":"2108246427931455764"},{"post_id":"2108181173499211993"},{"post_id":"2108235628693664241"},{"post_id":"2108326045648875879"},{"post_id":"2108271318802300928"},{"post_id":"2108181173499211993"},{"post_id":"2108277829422985694"}],"contexts":{"topics":["American Football"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"One post called pro athletes 'stupidly overpaid' at 500k a week, sparking hundreds of replies that flipped the script on who really benefits from sports billions.","id":"2107840624577655294","name":"Debate Heats Up Over Athlete Pay in Sports","summary":"A discussion on X questions if professional athletes earn too much amid economic pressures, with critics pointing to multimillion salaries while fans face rising costs. Defenders counter that players get just pennies from the revenue they generate—like the NBA's $11.68 billion in 2025-26 income, where athletes take about 51 percent under their agreement. Others highlight how owners and leagues keep most profits, with elite talent's scarcity justifying top pay in a capitalist entertainment world.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T00:01:44.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2107840624577655294"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108249687044264269"},{"post_id":"2108248649440375237"},{"post_id":"2108251155117604963"},{"post_id":"2108342916913475784"},{"post_id":"2108250924586323969"},{"post_id":"2108249687044264269"},{"post_id":"2108248649440375237"},{"post_id":"2108342916913475784"},{"post_id":"2108252678434312403"},{"post_id":"2108269061066903810"}],"contexts":{"topics":["MLB"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Imagine top teams handpicking their playoff foes, while the regular season shrinks back to 154 games for better player rest.","id":"2108251849614905520","name":"MLB Proposes 154-Game Season and Playoff Matchup Picks","summary":"Major League Baseball pitched changes during talks with the players' union: a shorter 154-game season with weekly off days starting in 2029, a best-of-seven Division Series that year, and higher seeds choosing Wild Card and Division opponents from 2027. The ideas aim to boost player health, create broadcast windows, and amp up October drama with more pitcher matchups and rivalries. Fans split on the matchup picks—some see fun storylines, others worry big clubs like the Yankees could game the system—while the union reviews amid salary cap talks before the CBA expires in December.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T06:47:38.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108251849614905520"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2107862120620511516"},{"post_id":"2108216053796897015"},{"post_id":"2107912016098668991"},{"post_id":"2108223758041293096"},{"post_id":"2107854527588077979"},{"post_id":"2107862120620511516"},{"post_id":"2108216053796897015"},{"post_id":"2107854527588077979"},{"post_id":"2107912016098668991"},{"post_id":"2107866299950842249"}],"contexts":{"topics":["American Football"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Young athletes like quarterback Carlos Spencer Jr. are turning heads with strong stats and fresh highlight reels, showing college coaches what they've got midway through the season.","id":"2107926667004105015","name":"High School Football Prospects Share Midseason Highlights to Boost Recruiting","summary":"Scouting site Six Star Football highlighted midseason risers posting impressive numbers and films from across the country, including West Coast talents against stunning backdrops. Standouts like Spencer with 1,739 passing yards, 24 touchdowns, and a 66% completion rate, Remy Vigne's 1,111 yards and 13 scores, and receiver Kye Wehby's 710 receiving yards lead the charge. These self-shared Hudl links and stats pair production with video to grab coaches' attention, with more expected as the season continues.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T01:33:04.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2107926667004105015"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108364857166762429"},{"post_id":"2108399623987470705"},{"post_id":"2108536484303347897"},{"post_id":"2108526242551247230"},{"post_id":"2108568416185438386"},{"post_id":"2108595911832273328"},{"post_id":"2108573387983659205"},{"post_id":"2108644690958430317"},{"post_id":"2108382166937968911"},{"post_id":"2108531389566234646"}],"contexts":{"topics":["MLB"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"A Dodgers fan in a Yamamoto jersey caught a foul ball in Game 3 of the NLDS at Truist Park. When asked to hand it to a young Braves fan nearby, he shrugged and said, 'I'm sorry, I can't. I'm not giving it to the kid.'","id":"2108453527047790840","name":"Dodgers Fan Keeps Foul Ball from Braves Kid, Dividing Baseball Fans","summary":"The clean catch during the playoff game at Truist Park led to a split in opinions, with some praising the fan for earning his souvenir fair and square and others saying he missed a chance to brighten a child's day. No MLB rule requires giving away foul balls caught in the stands, and the fan looked disappointed but kept it as his prize. The video spread widely, highlighting the ongoing tension between ballpark generosity and personal keepsakes.","updated_at":"2026-10-09T07:08:46.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108453527047790840"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108171737728762287"},{"post_id":"2108148149110132866"},{"post_id":"2108169122898923882"},{"post_id":"2108157815869366528"},{"post_id":"2108221491565273271"},{"post_id":"2108514511129137251"},{"post_id":"2108430223289045347"},{"post_id":"2108489214639640873"},{"post_id":"2108495938897489961"},{"post_id":"2108467513864388872"}],"contexts":{"topics":["Soccer"]},"disclaimer":"This story is a summary of posts on X and may evolve over time. Grok can make mistakes, verify its outputs.","hook":"Imagine turning a tiny stake into millions with one quick code. Bettors are posting SportyBet and Betway multibets loaded with 20-plus football picks, chasing odds in the hundreds of thousands.","id":"2108265220296589419","name":"Sports Bettors Share Multibet Codes for Huge Potential Payouts","summary":"Users share short codes like SportyBet's A7E845 or Betway's BW781B23E3 to instantly load accumulators with dozens of matches, focusing on markets like over 1.5 goals or both teams to score. These slips promise massive returns, such as R200k on a small bet or millions from a R1 wager on 35-leg bets with 859,000 odds. On October 8, posts surged with 'well booked' tickets and tips to edit or follow along, blending excitement over partial wins with reminders that most high-leg bets lose.","updated_at":"2026-10-08T18:45:26.000Z","url":"https://x.com/i/trending/2108265220296589419"},{"category":"Sports","cluster_posts_results":[{"post_id":"2108573205896282154"},{"post_id":"2108587098617819492"},{"post_id":"2108551674126086532"},{"post_id":"2108554906928054595"},{"post_id":"210854222258915346